Day 19 – Real-Time Retail Monitoring Dashboard using Streamlit

Objective

The objective of Day 19 was to develop a real-time retail monitoring dashboard using Streamlit. The dashboard integrates forecasting, inventory optimization, customer churn prediction, customer segmentation, and rolling sales statistics into a single interactive application for real-time business monitoring.

Dataset Overview

Multiple project datasets were imported into the dashboard, including Hybrid Forecast Results, Prophet Forecast, Inventory Optimization Results, Customer Churn Predictions, RFM Features, and Rolling Statistics. These datasets provide comprehensive insights into retail operations.

Dataset Features

The dashboard utilizes the following datasets and features:

- Hybrid Forecast Predictions
- Prophet Forecast
- Inventory Recommendations
- Customer Churn Probability
- RFM Customer Segmentation
- Rolling Sales Statistics

These datasets were combined to generate real-time business metrics and alerts.

Data Preparation

All required CSV files were loaded using Pandas. The dashboard was configured using Streamlit with a wide layout and dynamic page settings. The current date and time were displayed to indicate the latest dashboard update.

Dashboard Development

An interactive dashboard was developed using Streamlit. The dashboard includes KPI cards, business alerts, forecasting charts, inventory monitoring, customer churn analysis, customer segmentation, and rolling sales statistics.

Forecast Monitoring

Key forecasting metrics were displayed, including:

- Total Forecast
- Average Forecast
- Maximum Forecast
- Minimum Forecast

The dashboard automatically generated demand alerts when forecast values exceeded predefined thresholds.

Inventory Monitoring

Inventory metrics displayed include:

- Average Recommended Inventory
- Maximum Inventory
- Minimum Inventory

The dashboard also identified products with Low Stock status and generated inventory alerts.

Customer Churn Analysis

Customer churn metrics included:

- Total Customers
- Average Churn Probability
- High-Risk Customers

Automatic alerts were displayed whenever customers with high churn probability were detected.

Customer Segmentation

RFM metrics were presented to summarize customer behavior, including:

- Total Customers
- Average Purchase Frequency
- Average Monetary Value

These metrics help analyze customer purchasing patterns.

Rolling Sales Analysis

Rolling Mean and Rolling Standard Deviation charts were displayed to monitor sales trends and business volatility. Automatic alerts indicated whether sales remained stable or experienced significant fluctuations.

Interactive Tables

The dashboard displayed interactive tables for:

- Inventory Recommendations
- Customer Churn Predictions
- Hybrid Forecast Results

These tables enable users to review detailed business information directly within the application.

Key Findings

• Successfully integrated multiple project datasets into a single Streamlit dashboard.
• Displayed real-time forecasting KPIs.
• Generated automatic demand alerts.
• Monitored inventory levels and low-stock products.
• Displayed customer churn metrics and high-risk customer alerts.
• Presented customer segmentation statistics using RFM features.
• Visualized rolling sales trends and business volatility.
• Displayed interactive tables for inventory, churn prediction, and forecasting results.
• Developed a real-time business monitoring dashboard for retail analytics.

Conclusion

Day 19 focused on developing a Real-Time Retail Monitoring Dashboard using Streamlit. The application successfully integrated demand forecasting, inventory optimization, customer churn prediction, customer segmentation, and sales trend analysis into one interactive platform. The dashboard provides real-time KPIs, automated alerts, and detailed business insights, enabling efficient monitoring and data-driven decision-making for retail operations.